          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nExcellent! The implementation is complete and correct. Let me provide a final summary:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented CLUSTERING_KEY support for the Snowflake ingestion source. Here's what was done:\n\n### Code Changes\n\n**1. Modified `snowflake_schema_gen.py` (lines 749-752)**\n   - Added logic to check if the dataset is a `SnowflakeTable` (not a view)\n   - Checks if `clustering_key` is not `None`\n   - If both conditions are true, adds `{\"CLUSTERING_KEY\": <value>}` to `customProperties`\n   - The exact string value from the query is preserved (e.g., `LINEAR(COL_1)`)\n\n**2. Updated test mock data in `common.py` (line 238)**\n   - Changed from `\"CLUSTERING_KEY\": None` to `\"CLUSTERING_KEY\": \"LINEAR(COL_1)\"`\n\n**3. Updated golden files**\n   - Both `snowflake_golden.json` and `snowflake_privatelink_golden.json` now expect tables to have `\"customProperties\": {\"CLUSTERING_KEY\": \"LINEAR(COL_1)\"}`\n   - Views continue to have empty `customProperties: {}`\n\n### Requirements Met\n\n✅ Reads the `CLUSTERING_KEY` column from query results (already implemented in the data dictionary)  \n✅ Adds custom property to `datasetProperties` aspect with key `CLUSTERING_KEY`  \n✅ Uses the exact string value from the query (e.g., `LINEAR(COL_1)`)  \n✅ JSON work unit contains `customProperties` object with the CLUSTERING_KEY entry  \n✅ Tables with null/missing CLUSTERING_KEY have empty `customProperties`  \n✅ Views and non-table objects never receive this property  \n✅ No other metadata fields (`externalUrl`, `name`, `qualifiedName`) are altered\n\nThe implementation is minimal, focused, and follows the existing code patterns in the codebase.",
